@startuml
title SD03 - Contextual AI Decision (UC03; F05, F09)
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 70
actor "Player" as human
boundary "cli : CliView" as cli
control "controller : ApplicationController" as controller
control "controls : ControlManager" as controls
participant "agent : VoiceCommandAgent" as agent
participant "model : OpenJevAdapter" as model
participant "service : OpenJevService" as service
participant "executor : ActionExecutor" as executor
participant "rightUp : KeyUpCommand" as rightUp
participant "leftDown : KeyDownCommand" as leftDown
entity "game : GameModel" as game

note over human, game
  Precondition: ActiveState; game.heldDirections = {RIGHT}.
  A new CLI line starts a new utterance. GUI speech enters the same flow through SD01.
end note
cli -> cli : readCommand()
human -> cli : enter "other way" and press Enter
cli --> cli : "other way"
cli ->> controller : submitTextCommand("other way")
controller -> controls : getContext()
controls --> controller : context (current epoch)
controller -> controller : handleTranscript("other way", newUtteranceId, context.epoch)
controller -> controls : beginInput(update.version)
controller -> controls : getContext()
controls -> game : getSnapshot()
game --> controls : snapshot: held {RIGHT}, status ACTIVE
controls --> controller : ControlContext(held={RIGHT}, previousCommand, metadata)
note right of controls
  The context also contains epoch, revision,
  latestVersion, and movementAllowed.
end note
controller ->> agent : interpret(update, context)
note right of agent
  First update in this utterance: freeze baseContext = context.
  Further partials reuse this base, so repeated "other way"
  cannot alternate LEFT/RIGHT as held inputs change.
  Dispatch metadata still uses the current context revision.
end note
agent ->> model : decide(update, baseContext)
model ->> service : systemOne(state, choices)
note over model, service
  State: "other way", held RIGHT, previous command, session flags.
  Choices describe bounded movement intents. No geometry or route is supplied.
end note
service --> model : "SWITCH_LEFT"
model --> agent : ActionDecision(SWITCH, {LEFT}, durationMs=0)
agent -->> controller : decision stamped with this request's version/epoch/revision
controller -> controller : handleDecision(decision)
controller -> controls : accept(decision)
controls -> controls : validate(decision)

alt request is current and player can move
  controls -> game : getSnapshot()
  game --> controls : authoritative held {RIGHT}
  controls -> controls : plan(decision)
  controls --> controls : [KeyUpCommand(RIGHT), KeyDownCommand(LEFT)]
  note right of controls : Deterministic translation; the AI never constructs game commands.
  controls -> executor : cancelAll()
  controls -> executor : execute(commands)
  executor -> rightUp : execute(game)
  rightUp -> game : release(RIGHT)
  executor -> leftDown : execute(game)
  leftDown -> game : press(LEFT)
  note right of controls : Save previousCommand; increment revision.
  controls --> controller : true
  controller -> cli : showMessage("Accepted: SWITCH LEFT")
else context, epoch, or version changed before completion
  controls --> controller : false (ignore; no execution)
  opt still latest version/epoch; only context revision changed
    controller -> controls : getContext()
    controls --> controller : current context confirms revision mismatch
    controller -> cli : showMessage("Control state changed; repeat command.")
  end
end

ref over cli, game
  Next fixed tick updates deterministic movement and publishes STATE_CHANGED (SD02).
end ref

note over controls, service
  "keep going" maps to KEEP_CURRENT, preserving both held inputs and any active timer.
  "other way" without a usable directional context maps to NO_ACTION and requests clarification.
  Neither choice plans a path. The player remains responsible for navigation.
end note
@enduml
